[38;5;16m[48;5;153m ☐ Subscription [39m[49m

[1m[38;5;231mHow does a user express that they care about a task?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mDeclared watch, extensible matcher (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mExplicit per-task watch toggle. Subscriptions are stored records resolved by a single matcher function, so derived
[39m     [38;5;246mand rule-based subscriptions can be added later without touching event or delivery layers.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Derived from relationship
     [38;5;246mNo stored subscriptions — you're notified about tasks you created or are assigned. No UI, but notifies you about [39m
     [38;5;246meverything while there's only one user.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m Rule-based saved filters
     [38;5;246mSubscribe to queries (tag, due-soon, status) rather than individual tasks. Most expressive, covers future tasks, [39m
     [38;5;246mbut needs a matcher layer and rules UI up front.[39m
  [38;5;246m4. Type something.[39m
